# The slicing engine Spaghetti builds and serves (docs/slicer.md). Sourced by scripts/slicer/build.sh and read by the
# release workflow. Moving any of these means a new engine release (a `slicer-v*` tag) and a new engine.json.

# The Muon3D Slicer Engine: OrcaSlicer's libslic3r in WebAssembly, AGPL-3.0.
ENGINE_REPO=https://github.com/Muon-3D/muon3d-slicer-engine.git
ENGINE_TAG=v0.6.1
ENGINE_COMMIT=adaee71fcc81a851075867792bacd234d6bede35
# OrcaSlicer itself, upstream's release (not the engine's fork at 2.5.0-dev, whose orca/ submodule the engine's own build
# uses): the engine's checkout gets this tag, and scripts/slicer/engine.patch makes the engine build against it (CGAL 6,
# expat 2.10, no ClipperLib, the serial TBB shim's new functions). See docs/proposals/orcaslicer-2-5-1.md.
ORCA_REPO=https://github.com/OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer.git
ORCA_TAG=v2.5.1
ORCA_COMMIT=eef7710cb102fdb51a9bcdbd9efd61047f44774a
ORCA_VERSION=2.5.1

# The single-threaded engine is reproducible: a build of these commits and this patch must give these files, byte for
# byte, on any machine (an aarch64 sandbox gave the engine's own release hashes for its own pin; CI gives these). build.sh
# stops when it doesn't, unless SLICER_ALLOW_DIFFERENT=1.
ENGINE_ST_WASM_SHA256=bc74d6e3408e13ba0427e6555b0a97f43ec8675c37595fce64072f69d69697a6
ENGINE_ST_MJS_SHA256=32ef7543d26527ff9a2a5b8b1b0fabac53ccd8ef7b31466043bf29e8515636bd
